        <h2>Once You Know The Year</h2>

        <h3>Find Out What It's Worth</h3>
        <p>Dating a guitar is usually the first half of the question. The second half is what it's actually worth now, and that depends on the model, the year, the originality, and the finish far more than on the serial number.</p>
        <div class="chips">
          <a href="/vintage-fender-stratocaster-value-guide/">Stratocaster Value Guide</a>
          <a href="/vintage-fender-telecaster-value-guide/">Telecaster Value Guide</a>
          <a href="/free-appraisal/">Free Appraisal</a>
        </div>

        <h3>Go Deeper On Your Exact Guitar</h3>
        <p>If you've narrowed the year down, these go year by year through what a correct example should have, with photographs of the real thing.</p>
        <div class="chips">
          <a href="/post/1952-fender-telecaster-authentication-guide/">1952 Telecaster</a>
