          <a href="/post/fender-jazzmaster-evolution-guide-1958-1971/">Jazzmaster, 1958 To 1971</a>
          <a href="/post/fender-custom-color-authentication-guide/">Custom Colors And Finish</a>
        </div>
        <p class="note-sm mt">That's a selection rather than the whole shelf. There are more Fender guides on <a class="spoke" href="/blog/">the blog</a>, covering models and years not listed here, and I add to them as guitars come across the bench. If you can't find yours, <a class="spoke" href={hrefs.tel}>call or text me</a> and I'll point you at the right one.</p>

        <h3>Thinking About Selling</h3>
        <p>Joe buys vintage Fenders outright, pays on the spot, and covers shipping. No consignment wait and no auction fees.</p>
        <div class="chips">
